		<h2>Lesson Plans</h2>
		<hr/>
		<p>The American Congress Digital Archives Portal is a selection of personal papers from elected members of Congress. Because of this, resources do not necessarily include the bills themselves, but they do include records on how the representatives were considering voting and how their constituents thought about them. They offer a behind-the-scenes view of lawmaking often left out of history textbooks.
			These resources invite student-centered learning and research opportunities through encouraging choice and voice in research topics and exploration of primary source materials. Use of archival materials also offers students practice in inquiry-based approaches and historical thinking skills like perspective taking with analysis of constituent letters and comparing and contrasting debated concerns.</p>
		<h3> Elementary School </h3>
			<hr />
		<section class="static-cards-resources my-5">
			<div class="container" style="padding-left: 0px;">
				<div class="row g-4 justify-content-start">
					<div class="col-12 col-md-4 col-lg-4">
						<%= link_to '/downloads/2Link_LetterWritingLessonPlan.docx', download: '2Link_LetterWritingLessonPlan.docx', class: "card carousel-card d-block text-reset text-decoration-none shadow-sm", style: "height: 500px;" do %>
							<%= image_tag 'cards/Elementary_Photo.png', class: 'card-img-top', alt: 'Letter Writing Photo' %>
							<div class="card-body">
								<h4 class="card-title text-start">Elementary Constituent Writing</h4>
								<p class="card-text">This 3-day unit focuses on student learning who their representatives are in Congress and the importance of writing to them. The lessons are grounded in the inquiry question: How do our representatives know what we care about?</p>
							</div>
						<% end %>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>
		

		<h3> Middle School </h3>
			<hr />
<section class="static-cards-resources my-5">
	<div class="container" style="padding-left: 0px;">
		<div class="row g-4 justify-content-start">

			<!-- Card 1 -->
			<div class="col-12 col-md-4 col-lg-4">
				<%= link_to '/downloads/Middle_School_Civil_Rights.docx', download: 'Middle_School_Civil_Rights.docx', class: "card carousel-card d-block text-reset text-decoration-none shadow-sm", style: "height: 500px;" do %>
					<%= image_tag 'cards/Middle_School_Card.png', class: 'card-img-top', alt: 'Middle School Screencap' %>
					<div class="card-body">
						<h4 class="card-title text-start">Middle School Civil Rights</h4>
						<p class="card-text">Designed as an Inquiry Design Model, this lesson will help students to understand that the desire to increase civil rights for Americans has occurred across American history and is not only tied to the national fight for rights during the 1950s and 1960s. The sources selected for this lesson were collected with middle-grade learners in mind.</p>
					</div>
				<% end %>
			</div>

			<!-- Card 2 -->
			<div class="col-12 col-md-4 col-lg-4">
				<%= link_to '/downloads/2Link_IndianEducationLessonPlan.docx', download: '2Link_IndianEducationLessonPlan.docx', class: "card carousel-card d-block text-reset text-decoration-none shadow-sm", style: "height: 500px;" do %>
					<%= image_tag 'cards/MS Indian Education.png', class: 'card-img-top', alt: 'Middle School Indian Education Photo' %>
					<div class="card-body">
						<h4 class="card-title text-start">Middle School Civil Rights: Indian Education</h4>
						<p class="card-text">This lesson is intended to offer a supplementary Civil Rights lesson for middle school students, directly aligned with the American Congress Digital Archives Portal Inquiry Design Model (IDM) lesson on Civil Rights. It remains focused on the compelling question: What does it take to become a “more perfect union?”</p>
					</div>
				<% end %>
			</div>

			<!-- Card 3 -->
			<div class="col-12 col-md-4 col-lg-4">
				<%= link_to '/downloads/2Link_CampaignAnalysisLessonPlan.docx', download: '2Link_CampaignAnalysisLessonPlan.docx', class: "card carousel-card d-block text-reset text-decoration-none shadow-sm", style: "height: 500px;" do %>
					<%= image_tag 'cards/MS Campaign Analysis.png', class: 'card-img-top', alt: 'Middle School Campaign Analysis Photo' %>
					<div class="card-body">
						<h4 class="card-title text-start">Middle School Campaign Analysis</h4>
						<p class="card-text">This 3-day middle school-focused lesson examines the strategies used in both historical and modern campaign advertisements. With a focus on critical thinking, students will learn to consider the persuasion methods that campaigns use with the voting public. Through learning to use a critical lens to analyze political media, students can then practice transferring that lens to social media and the world around them.</p>
					</div>
				<% end %>
			</div>

		</div>
	</div>
</section>

		<h3> High School</h3>
			<hr />
		<section class="static-cards-3 my-5">
			<div class="container" style="padding-left: 0px;">
				<div class="row g-4 justify-content-start">
